---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Main from "../components/Main.astro";

export const prerender = true;

const title = "TasteBuddy for Claude | TasteBuddy";
const description =
  "Connect TasteBuddy to Claude to search your recipes, plan meals, and add items to your shopping list from a Claude conversation.";

const readTools = [
  ["Search recipes", "Find recipes saved in your account and shared with your household."],
  ["Get a recipe", "Read one recipe with its ingredients, sections, and steps."],
  ["List cookbooks", "See your cookbooks and how many recipes each holds."],
  ["Get cookbook recipes", "List the recipes in one cookbook."],
  ["Get shopping list", "Read the shared household shopping list."],
  ["Get meal plan", "Read the planned meals for a week (Monday to Sunday)."],
];

const writeTools = [
  ["Save recipe", "Save a new recipe, for example one Claude found or wrote with you."],
  ["Add to shopping list", "Add items to the household shopping list."],
  ["Add to meal plan", "Plan a meal on a date."],
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Main>
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-12 text-gray-300 sm:py-16">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[#00CE31]">Connector</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold text-white sm:text-4xl">TasteBuddy for Claude</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        The TasteBuddy connector lets Claude work with your recipes, cookbooks, meal plan, and shopping list. Ask
        things like "what can I cook from my saved pasta recipes?", "plan the lentil soup for Friday dinner", or
        "add everything I need for it to my shopping list".
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Connect TasteBuddy</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 leading-7">
        <li>In Claude, open <strong class="text-white">Settings → Connectors</strong> and search for TasteBuddy.</li>
        <li>Select <strong class="text-white">Connect</strong>.</li>
        <li>
          Sign in to TasteBuddy if asked, check that the request comes from Claude
          (<code class="text-[#00CE31]">claude.ai</code>), and select <strong class="text-white">Approve</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>In a conversation, make sure TasteBuddy is turned on in the tools menu.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        You need a TasteBuddy account. The connector works in Claude on the web, the desktop apps, and mobile once
        connected.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-white">What Claude can do</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">Claude only sees data your TasteBuddy account can see, including data shared with your household.</p>
      <h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-white">Read</h3>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3">
        {readTools.map(([name, text]) => (
          <li class="rounded-lg border border-[#2A2D24] bg-[#10130B] p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold text-white">{name}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 leading-6">{text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-white">Add</h3>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3">
        {writeTools.map(([name, text]) => (
          <li class="rounded-lg border border-[#2A2D24] bg-[#10130B] p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold text-white">{name}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 leading-6">{text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        Claude asks before it adds anything. The connector cannot edit or delete existing recipes, list items, or
        plans, and it cannot place grocery orders.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Disconnect</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        In Claude, open <strong class="text-white">Settings → Connectors → TasteBuddy</strong> and select
        <strong class="text-white">Disconnect</strong>. To have us revoke the access on our side as well,
        <a class="text-[#00CE31] underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-7">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Connected, but Claude finds no TasteBuddy tools:</strong> disconnect and connect
          again so Claude reloads the tool list.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">The approval page asks you to sign in:</strong> sign in in the tab that opens,
          then return to the approval page. It continues automatically.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Something else:</strong>
          <a class="text-[#00CE31] underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href="/contact/">contact us</a> and include
          the time it happened.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Privacy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        TasteBuddy does not receive or store your Claude conversations. When Claude uses a tool, TasteBuddy sends
        the requested data to Claude. See section 4 of our
        <a class="text-[#00CE31] underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </Main>
</Layout>
